extraction_notes: |
  - Transcribed from printed 74-76 (cache p075-p077); the bonus lines, the
    P.P.E. line and the XP ladder were read off renders. The ladder is the
    "Conjurer, Controller Magus" column on printed 160, shared with the
    Conjurer; xp_table holds each band''s lower bound.
  - The text layer prints the P.P.E. base as 1D4xIO+X (a substituted digit);
    the render reads 1D4x10+8.
  - The attribute minimums are printed under an "Alignment Restrictions" label,
    a misprint: the book states no alignment restriction for the Controller.
  - The three spells of choice at level one come from spell levels 1-4. A few
    extra spells learned outside his career are seldom more than 1D4+2.
    Automatons carry their own spells; see each automaton''s vehicles row.
  - "+1 to save vs mind control and possession at levels 1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11,
    13 and 15" and "+1 to save vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 11,
    13 and 15" are carried in bonuses.saves (level one) and at_level. "+1 to
    save vs magic" is flat.
  - The automaton bond, the bonuses a bonded Automaton gets, and the Automatons
    he starts bonded to are prose: they belong to the construct, not the
    character sheet. The Automatons are vehicles rows (slugs named in the
    special abilities), and a character owns one through character_vehicles.
  - The body armor (35 M.D.C.) and helmet (35 M.D.C.), the TW flashlight and
    the weapons (two ancient of choice, one ancient-style magic or TW weapon,
    one conventional) have no catalog rows and stay in the Equipment section;
    the flashlight is the plain flashlight row.
  - men_of_arms is false: the book files the class under its "Magus O.C.C.s"
    heading (printed 70), a school of magic, as a sub-set of the Battle Magus.
---

## Lore

The Controller is a sub-set of the Battle Magus, trained by the same Brotherhood of Battle. He sacrifices some of his personal combat ability to link himself physically and mentally to one or more Automatons, and is to them what a power armor pilot is to his suit, relying on his own mind and magic rather than machines. Some Controllers sleep in the pilot area of their construct or cradled in its arms. Killing the Controller renders his Automaton inert, though another Magus can pilot it or a new Controller can be bonded to it. For every ten Battle Magi there is one Controller.

Like the Battle Magus, the Controller enjoys combat, especially against giant monsters, dragons, robots and power armor, and is a formidable combatant even without an Automaton.

## Equipment

Clothes, utility belt, two canteens, backpack, knapsack, three weeks of food rations, a pair of handcuffs, 50 feet (15.2 m) of strong cord or rope, 1D4 flares, a TW flashlight and a pocket knife.

Standard Controller body armor (35 M.D.C.) and helmet (35 M.D.C.) of M.D.C. polycarbonate plates and padding or magically created materials; no metal, not a full environmental suit.

Weapons: two ancient of choice (no special powers), one ancient-style magic or TW weapon and one conventional weapon, plus his Earth Thunder Automaton (and the Infiltrator and others on special assignment).

Money: as a member of the Dweomer Defense Force he has a furnished two-bedroom apartment, meals, uniforms, healing and access to the academies, plus 600 Universal Credits a month. Starts with 3D4x100 credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-magus-controller');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'battle-magus-controller';

